const COUNTER_EVENT = 'Directed counterevidence: no study was found showing that a first exposure to a new strength exercise days before a race is harmless or that it is harmful at a 1-set, RIR 3-4 dose; the time trial of Devantier-Thomas 2024 was unchanged 24-48 h after a heavy first bout, so the risk of a light first exposure is directional and small, not quantified. The protection a prior bout gives is task-specific (Maeo 2017) and wanes over 9-12 weeks (Theodorou 2026), which limits what a stand-in performed long ago carries. No open-access synthesis on two-to-three-week strength retention was found (negative search logged).';
