// ---------- findings (text shared by records and the markdown) ----------
const F11 = 'R7B1-SSCTR-F11 (MODERATE; non-blocking for this gate; inherited, not in the delta): an EQUIPMENT_CHANGE reported for the event weeks (permanent, or a dated window such as travel to the race) puts same-intent configurations never performed in this program on TAPER, RACE_WEEK and POST_EVENT days (s02: all 15 well-formed reports of 3 athletes, 94 rows, all 1 set at RIR >= 3 in the taper and >= 4 on race and post-event days, effort-established or bodyweight, e.g. kb-deadlift 1 x 5-10 in the taper after a switch to kettlebell only). Same rule family as QE-R7B-OBS-04 (R6-EVENT-TRANSITION C7, B0-C05 c1), but not a reason-based substitution, byte-identical on FREEZE-2, and inside the literal R6-SUBSTITUTION envelope ("when equipment or circumstance removes an exercise") and its first-exposure dose (C6: at most 2 sets at RIR >= 3). Required change (next runtime mission): on event-phase days an equipment-forced substitute this program has not performed gives way to a performed configuration that fits the equipment of the date (the same stand-in rule), otherwise the slot is left out and disclosed (R6-SUBSTITUTION C8); the substitute starts after the post-event week with its establishment.';
const F12 = 'R7B1-SSCTR-F12 (MINOR; non-blocking; on the R7-B.1 path; no dose effect): a substitution decided before the event weeks whose substitute is planned before them (the last SPECIFIC week) shows that substitute in the taper of its conditional projection and carries no NO_NEW_EXERCISE_IN_EVENT_WEEKS disclosure (68 decisions in s01). When the weekly review of that week finds the substitute not performed, it correctly leaves the slot out of the event weeks or uses a performed stand-in, but returns no disclosure: a slot left out is recorded only in the session\'s structured eventStandIns (s04), while R6-SUBSTITUTION C8 asks that the omission be disclosed. Required change: the decision says the substitute enters the event weeks only once done before them, and a review that leaves a slot out of an event-phase session discloses it as the substitution decision does.';
